rupees, &ldquo;MXN&rdquo; means Mexican pesos, &ldquo;RUB&rdquo; means Russian roubles and &ldquo;U.S.$&rdquo; means U.S. dollars.</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0 0 0 14.2pt; text-align: justify"><I>&nbsp;</I></P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 0"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 14.2pt"><SUP>(2)</SUP></TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">&ldquo;CDI&rdquo; means the Brazilian interbank deposit rate (Certificado de Dep&oacute;sito Interbanc&aacute;rio),
&ldquo;SOFR&rdquo; means Secured Overnight Financing rate, &ldquo;TIIE&rdquo; means the Equilibrium Inter-banking Interest Rate (Tasa
de Inter&eacute;s Interbancaria de Equilibrio), and &ldquo;T-bill&rdquo; means the India Treasury bill interest rate.</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><I>&nbsp;</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Summary of statements of cash flows</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify">The following table summarizes our statements of cash
flows for the periods presented:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

